35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: I found the complaint log. Eleven of fourteen complaints came from the house with the gate. That explains a lot of the tension.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: I visited the station block’s bin house. The smell is worse than the open pile, and they argue constantly about sweeping.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The clerk says a permanent build needs four months and five signatures. Supervised mornings average fifty minutes, so we’d each take twenty a year.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I measured the frontages. One is crossed by a driveway, and the narrowest leaves only ninety centimetres. The complaint log confirms the gate household filed eleven of fourteen complaints.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The ledger shows thirty-four thousand yen yearly in extra fees, and the subsidy covers only forty percent of a two hundred forty-eight thousand yen build.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Rin, that confirms it. The gate household is the loudest, but the measurements show the space is genuinely tight. We need a plan that respects those limits.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Asuka, twenty supervised mornings a year is a lot. I worry we will lose our peace over who is on duty.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, it is manageable if we rotate fairly. The real issue is the four-month delay for a permanent build. We need a faster, less intrusive solution.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, the driveway and the ninety-centimetre gap prove it. We cannot just build a wall there. We need a plan that moves the burden around.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, forty percent is a small comfort against two hundred forty-eight thousand. We must ask if we can truly afford the remaining sixty percent, or if we are setting ourselves up for debt.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: @Servas, if the money is tight, maybe we shouldn’t build anything permanent. I just want us to keep talking without shouting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Kenji, I agree. A permanent structure brings permanent arguments, as the station block learned. Let us seek a gentler path that preserves our harmony.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the cost is prohibitive. But the rotation option avoids the four-month delay and the construction debt entirely. It is the only logical path forward.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, rotation sounds fair, but with a driveway and ninety-centimetre gaps, moving it constantly might just create new messes.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you are right to be cautious. Yet, if we avoid the debt, we preserve our peace. Let us weigh the movement against the cost of standing still.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I hear you. But if we don’t move it, the gate household keeps suffering. Maybe we can find a middle ground that keeps us all talking?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, a middle ground sounds wise. Perhaps we can rotate gently, avoiding the tightest spots, so no one feels trapped or burdened.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, the measurements show the physical limits, but the rotation schedule can simply exclude the driveway and the narrowest frontage. We only rotate among the viable spaces.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that’s clever. If we skip the impossible spots, rotation actually works. I’m in, as long as the schedule is published and fixed.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, a fixed schedule is the anchor we need. It turns uncertainty into routine, allowing us to breathe and trust one another again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
