61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: I agree, Kenji. A gentle rotation, avoiding the tight spots, seems the kindest way to share the burden without causing new friction.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,- **Asuka**: I support rotation. It avoids the construction debt and the four-month delay. We simply exclude the driveway and the narrowest frontage from the schedule.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,I support rotation too. It’s the only way to stop one family from carrying the weight. Let’s make sure the schedule is clear and fair for everyone.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"I concur. A shared rhythm, free of debt and delay, allows us to move forward together with dignity and mutual respect.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,- **Kenji**: I’m ready to vote for rotation. It feels like the best chance for us to stay friends and keep this lane peaceful.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: I vote for rotation. It feels the most gentle and fair, allowing us to share the burden without causing new friction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"I vote for rotation. It is the only option that balances the financial constraints with a workable, time-efficient schedule.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
